# interplay_boot_20: A guest's whole life (pgtest/boot_util.py): each seed is one scenario, interplay_boot_<seed>, whose program the generator builds from the seed alone: one device session that goes through the phases a macOS guest goes through under QEMU's apple-gfx, end to end, with every subsystem busy where a real guest's would be.  The firmware's EFI frames on port 0's display (at version 0, before the driver, or after its version negotiation); the driver's takeover (version negotiation, root page and root FIFO, task 0, device info, child FIFOs, the gate and GPU tasks, EFI turned off, each head's shared page connected and acked, the cursor's glyph, show and position); the window server (the IOSurface host device's ring and table, mapper surfaces, a compositor task with a mapper buffer over each); steady state (the GPU copies a window into a surface and the compositor presents it with opcode 8 from a FIFO behind the copy, opcode-7 presents of task 0's backings, gamma tables, colour matrices, ICC profiles, cursor moves and glyphs, beside the marathon's app batches, app faults and their recovery, lifetime and memory changes); the host hot-plugging displays and setting mode lists, each update acked; the heads put to sleep, presents while asleep, woken; a host pause now and then; the suspend onto a fresh device, with work held on the gate across it, and steady state after the resume; and the shutdown: everything released and compared, cursors hidden, heads disconnected, the compositor's buffers and task deleted, the surfaces unmapped, the backings deleted, the child FIFOs, the gate and every task deleted, the root FIFO disabled, and the device released, or reset and booted to the firmware's EFI frames again. Before each phase ends the seed decides what is busy (work held on the gate, work running free, a faulted child, EFI frames).  The model is the display walk's and the marathon's (pgtest/randdisplay.py, pgtest/marathon_util.py), extended to the compositor's copies: every callback, interrupt, shared page, encoded pixel, present count, GPU slot, scratch page, surface and fault register is predicted, and every wait succeeds but those labelled [held] and [dies]; python3 -m pgtest.boot_util reads the expected files back against it. Programs with mapper surfaces run in the map and isolate setups, the others in all three. Some programs stop at a realistic moment in a death docs/testing.md 7.3 and 7.4 list, with work held on the gate: a one-entry gamma table in steady state, a guest mode count over 128 when the host sets a new list, rvg_display_cursor_position while the host has the device paused in the sleep phase, and at the suspend the cursor doorbell while paused or a second pause.  This program: 1 port, mapper surfaces and a compositor, EFI after the version, GPU set-up after EFI goes off, 2 children, 2 tasks; steady 16/4/10; ack 2, compose 11, connect 1, cursor 1, efi frame 1, gpu 11, hotplug replug 1, misc compositor 1, misc encode 1, move 4, release 2; ends in a death (mode_count_over).
